---
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import PageMain from '../components/PageMain.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const UPDATED = '13 October 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="What happens to the details you send through the contact form."
>
	<PageHeader
		title="Privacy Policy"
		subtitle="What happens to the details you send through the Party Chat form."
	/>

	<PageMain>
		<Panel kicker="// 01 - WHAT I COLLECT" title="What I collect">
			<Fragment slot="intro">
				The only place on this site where you can send me information is the
				form on the <a class="policy__link" href="/contact">Party Chat</a>
				page. I am William (Spimy), based in Mauritius, and I am the person responsible
				for what you send there.
			</Fragment>

			<ul class="policy__list" role="list">
				<li>
					<strong>Your name, email address and message.</strong> You type these in
					yourself, and the form needs all three. You do not have to use the form:
					the other links on the contact page work too.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Your IP address.</strong> The site uses it to limit how many messages
					one person can send in an hour, and passes it to hCaptcha to check that
					you are not a bot. It is kept in the server's memory only, not in a database.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>hCaptcha.</strong> With JavaScript on, the form uses hCaptcha, a
					security service from Intuition Machines, Inc. (a US company), to check
					that you are a person and not a bot. It is loaded when you open the <a
						class="policy__link"
						href="/contact">contact page</a
					>, and shows you a short challenge when you send a message. It looks
					at information such as your IP address, how long you have been on the
					page and your mouse movements, and sends it to Intuition Machines.
					This may start before the challenge appears. I use it only to protect
					the form from spam and abuse. hCaptcha acts on my behalf as a data
					processor, and its{' '}
					<a class="policy__link" href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy"
						>Privacy Policy</a
					>{' '}
					and{' '}
					<a class="policy__link" href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/terms"
						>Terms of Service</a
					>{' '}
					apply. Without JavaScript, the form uses a hidden check instead, which sends
					nothing to hCaptcha.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is hosted on Vercel, which may log
					basic details of each visit, such as the IP address, as part of running
					the site.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p class="policy__text">
				I use your name, email and message only to read your message and, if I
				reply, to write back to you.
			</p>
		</Panel>

		<Panel kicker="// 02 - WHERE IT GOES" title="Where it goes" tone="soft">
			<ul class="policy__list" role="list">
				<li>
					<strong>It becomes an email.</strong> Your message is sent through Microsoft's
					email service (Office 365) to my inbox. It is not saved in any database
					on this site, so the only copy is the one in my inbox.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>One short exception.</strong> If you send a message without JavaScript,
					the site keeps your name and message in the server's memory for up to 5
					minutes so it can show them back to you after the page reloads. They are
					forgotten as soon as they are shown, or when the time runs out.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>How long I keep it.</strong> If we end up in a real conversation,
					such as with a recruiter or a freelance client, I keep it and archive it
					as a record. Anything else, like spam or a casual hello, I almost always
					delete as soon as I have replied, if I reply at all.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Outside Mauritius.</strong> Microsoft, hCaptcha and Vercel are international
					services, so some of your data may be processed outside Mauritius.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</Panel>

		<Panel kicker="// 03 - YOUR CHOICES" title="Your choices" tone="pop">
			<ul class="policy__list" role="list">
				<li>
					You can ask what I hold about you, ask me to correct it, or ask me to
					delete it.
				</li>
				<li>
					You can take back your consent at any time by asking me to delete your
					message.
				</li>
				<li>
					To do any of this, write to me using the <strong>Show email</strong> button
					on the{' '}
					<a class="policy__link" href="/contact#links">contact page</a>.
				</li>
				<li>
					If you are not happy with how I handled your data, you can complain to
					the Data Protection Commissioner in Mauritius, through the{' '}
					<a class="policy__link" href="https://dataprotection.govmu.org"
						>Data Protection Office</a
					>.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p class="policy__text">
				If this changes, I will update this page and the date below.
			</p>
			<p class="policy__updated">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>
		</Panel>
	</PageMain>
</Layout>

<style>
	.policy__list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.875rem;
		max-width: 64ch;
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
		padding: 0 0 0 1.125rem;
		list-style: disc;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	.policy__list li::marker {
		color: var(--accent-pop);
	}

	.policy__list strong {
		color: var(--text);
	}

	.policy__text {
		max-width: 64ch;
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	.policy__link {
		color: var(--accent-soft);
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
	}

	.policy__link:hover {
		color: var(--text);
	}

	.policy__updated {
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
</style>
